 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Roughly one liter per hour. Are you going anywhere tough, like heat and distance? Then good practice is to take a little more than you think you need. Wanting a drink is much easier than being thirsty. If it' short ride, a bar or energy gel can keep you going. But if it' long, a full drink every hour is decent advice. Some people can, but it's few and far between. Your body needs fuel, and it's easy to miss it.",
